Ta có: $\sin(3\pi-\alpha) = \sin(\pi-\alpha+2\pi) = \sin(\pi-\alpha) = \sin\alpha$ ;
$\sin\left(\alpha+\dfrac{5\pi}{2}\right) = \sin\left(\alpha+\dfrac{\pi}{2}+2\pi\right) = \sin\left(\alpha+\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right) = \cos(-\alpha) = \cos\alpha$.
Suy ra $\sin^2(3\pi-\alpha) + \sin^2\left(\alpha+\dfrac{5\pi}{2}\right) = \sin^2\alpha + \cos^2\alpha = 1$.
